# Line-ending policy.
#
# Without this file git guesses, and it guessed wrong about the PDF fixtures
# under backend/test-fixtures/: it reported "LF will be replaced by CRLF the
# next time Git touches it" for files whose bytes are not text. A PDF with its
# line endings rewritten is a corrupt PDF, so `npm test` would have passed on
# the machine that committed the fixtures and failed on the next clone — the
# worst shape a test failure can take, because it looks like a real defect in
# code that never changed.
#
# Text files are normalised to LF in the repository and checked out however the
# platform prefers. Anything listed as binary is left exactly as it is.

* text=auto

# Never touch these — the bytes are the content.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4   binary
*.zip   binary

# Shell scripts must keep LF even when checked out on Windows: a CRLF shebang
# line is not a shebang, and the script fails with a message that names the
# interpreter rather than the line ending.
*.sh    text eol=lf
